user Steve Leffler @physics.u writes:
>   One thing about hack that I'm not clear on is the aggravate monster
>intrinsic.  I seem to see it come up a lot when I die and view my intrinsics.
>Besides eating your dog or wearing a ring of aggravate monster, how do you
>get this intrinsic?  What exactly does it do? I know it makes the monster
>problem worse somehow, but how?  Most importantly, once you've got it,
is there
>any way of getting rid of it?

I think you can get it from a cursed potion of invisibility ("Your
presence seems known") and a spellbook ("You feel threatened"), but I
don't know if these are permanent.  Sorry about my lack of info.

What I can answer is this last question.  In early version of nethack
(maybe it was just hack), if you ate something that made you vomit there
was a chance you lost a random intrinsic.  There was no particular
garuantee you'd lose aggrivate monster, but hey, what the heck? 
Unfortunately, this avenue is no longer available (actually, that's
good...bum tins would be a real pain in the butt).  The only way I know
of to ditch an intrinsic (unless you count stuff like losing telepathy
by attacking a shopkeeper when you're lawful) is to have a gremlin swipe
it.  This is only for somebody who is really desperate...if the gremlins
are anything like nymphs, they'll steal all the good intrinsics and
leave you with ONLY aggrivate monster (ever notice how nymphs always
seem to grab your only decent weapons and armor and then leave you
facing an orc horde?).  Plus, if you're in hell, the little piker will
probably steal fire resistance (don't laugh, my best knight ever died
this way).

